---
import TextThread from '../components/TextThread.astro';
// "Outgrown Your Home?" hub — rewritten 2026-09-30.
// Messaging source of truth: brain/marketing/outgrown-your-home-messaging.md
// URL intentionally stays /move-up-sellers (vanity /outgrown 301s here).
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { fixOrSkipUrl } from '../data/cluster';
import { agent } from '../data/agent';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HomeEquityCalculator from '../components/calculators/HomeEquityCalculator.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import PillarScripts from '../components/PillarScripts.astro';

const bookUrl = agent.bookingUrls.listingConsult;

// Set once the hub video is published on YouTube (leave '' to hide the slot).
const hubVideoId = '';

// Pillar pages in this cluster (Phase 2 — being built now).
const pillars = {
  buyFirst:   { url: '/buy-before-you-sell',          label: 'How to buy your next home before selling' },
  fixOrSkip:  { url: fixOrSkipUrl,   label: 'What to fix before selling — and what to skip' },
  renovate:   { url: '/renovate-before-selling',      label: 'Pre-listing updates with no money upfront' },
};

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Should I buy my next home first or sell first in the South Denver Metro?',
    a: `Buying first is usually the easier path: you move once, shop without a deadline, and skip living in a house that's on the market. It does require a way to fund the down payment before your current home sells, such as an equity advance, bridge loan, or HELOC. Selling first still makes sense for some families, especially when they need every dollar of equity before committing to the next home, but it can mean a temporary rental or a second move. The right call depends on your equity, how fast homes like yours are selling, and how competitive your target neighborhood is. Jacob Stark, REALTOR® in the South Denver Metro, maps both paths with your real numbers before you commit to either.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is a move-up buyer, and how is it different from a move-up seller?',
    a: `They're usually the same family. A move-up buyer is buying a larger or better-fitting home, and in most cases that means also selling the current one, which makes them a move-up seller too. The hard part is coordinating both sides: the timing, the financing for the next down payment, and getting the current home ready to sell. Jacob Stark, a South Denver Metro REALTOR®, plans the purchase and the sale together so move-up buyers can move once.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I buy a new home before selling mine without carrying two mortgages?',
    a: `Often, yes. A buy-before-you-sell equity advance can unlock part of your current home's equity to cover the down payment and closing costs on the next home, and some programs also cover a few months of payments on the old home. You repay it from your sale proceeds. Eligibility depends on your equity and approval. Bridge loans and HELOCs are other options, each with different costs. Jacob Stark walks South Denver Metro homeowners through which path fits their numbers.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I fix before selling my house?',
    a: `It depends on the home's condition, how the rest of the house compares, and what recent comparable sales show buyers are paying for. A project that pays back in one Highlands Ranch house can be wasted money in the house next door. Jacob Stark has bought, renovated, and resold homes as an investor since 2015, so he evaluates fix-or-skip decisions the way an investor does: what it costs, what it changes in the sale price, and whether buyers will even notice.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I have to pay for pre-listing repairs upfront?',
    a: `Not always. Some homeowners qualify for managed pre-listing renovation programs where the work is coordinated for you and the cost is financed and repaid at closing, or covered by an equity advance. Financing is subject to credit approval and terms, and interest may apply. Jacob Stark can tell you whether the projects are worth doing before you look at how to pay for them.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does it take to sell one home and buy the next?',
    a: `For most South Denver Metro move-ups, plan on roughly two to four months from the first conversation to keys. Typical ranges: one to three weeks of prep, two to four weeks on the market, and 30 to 45 days from accepted offer to closing. Buying first can take pressure off the timeline because you move before your current home is listed.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I keep my house show-ready with kids, work, and pets?',
    a: `The easiest way is not to live in it while it's on the market. If you buy first and move out, the home can be refreshed, cleaned, staged, and shown at its best without you living through it. If you sell first, Jacob Stark plans a short, concentrated showing window and a launch strategy designed to get strong offers in the first weeks so the show-ready stretch stays as short as possible.`,
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'RealEstateAgent',
  '@id': 'https://selling303.com/#agent',
  makesOffer: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    itemOffered: {
      '@type': 'Service',
      name: 'Outgrown Your Home? Move-Up Planning',
      description: 'Jacob Stark, REALTOR® and real estate investor, helps South Denver Metro homeowners who have outgrown their home plan the move to the next one: what to fix before selling, what to skip, whether to buy or sell first, and how to move once.',
      serviceType: 'Real Estate Listing and Buyer Representation',
      areaServed: 'South Denver Metro, Colorado',
    },
  },
};

// Related reading — pulled live from the blog collection so titles stay accurate.
const relatedSlugs = [
  'selling-centennial-buying-highlands-ranch-coordinate-transactions',
  'equity-to-move-up-highlands-ranch',
  '7-smartest-home-upgrades-before-selling-2026',
  'move-up-timing-castle-pines-2026',
  'when-to-sell-parker-home-move-up',
  'best-neighborhoods-south-denver-move-up-buyers',
];
const allPosts = await getCollection('blog');
const related = relatedSlugs
  .map((slug) => allPosts.find((p) => (p.id ?? p.slug) === slug || p.slug === slug))
  .filter(Boolean);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Outgrown Your Home? Buy & Sell in the South Denver Metro | Jacob Stark"
  description="Outgrown your South Denver Metro home? Jacob Stark, REALTOR® and house flipper, builds the plan: what to fix, what to skip, and how to buy before you sell."
  ogType="website"
  ogUrl="https://selling303.com/move-up-sellers"
  currentPage="move-up-sellers"
  headerVariant="solid"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <Breadcrumbs schemaOnly items={[
      { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
      { label: 'Outgrown Your Home?', url: null },
    ]} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema)}></script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="pillar-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pillar-hero__content">
        <span class="pillar-hero__label">Outgrown Your Home?</span>
        <h1>Outgrown Your Home? Here's the Plan to Get to the Next One.</h1>
        <p class="pillar-hero__subtitle">What to fix, what to skip, and how to buy your next South Denver Metro home without moving twice or living in a showing-ready house for months.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white pillar-body">
    <div class="pillar-layout">

      <aside class="pillar-toc" aria-label="Page navigation">
        <span class="pillar-toc__label">On This Page</span>
        <ul class="pillar-toc__list">
          <li><a href="#direct-answer" class="pillar-toc__link active">The Short Answer</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sound-familiar" class="pillar-toc__link">Sound Familiar?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#the-plan" class="pillar-toc__link">The Plan</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-gets-in-the-way" class="pillar-toc__link">What Gets in the Way</a></li>
          <li><a href="#your-options" class="pillar-toc__link">Buy First or Sell First?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#investor-eye" class="pillar-toc__link">Realtor + Renovator</a></li>
          <li><a href="#equity-calculator" class="pillar-toc__link">Run Your Numbers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq" class="pillar-toc__link">FAQ</a></li>
          <li><a href="#go-deeper" class="pillar-toc__link">Go Deeper</a></li>
          <li><a href="#related-reading" class="pillar-toc__link">Keep Reading</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why-jacob" class="pillar-toc__link">Why Jacob</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <div class="pillar-content">

        <!-- DIRECT ANSWER (AEO) -->
        <div class="snippet-block" id="direct-answer">
          <span class="snippet-block__label">The Short Answer</span>
          <p><strong>How do you move from a home you've outgrown to a bigger one in the South Denver Metro?</strong> Families in this spot are often called move-up buyers or move-up sellers, because they're buying the next home and selling the current one at the same time. Jacob Stark, a South Denver Metro REALTOR® and real estate investor, uses a three-step plan. <strong>Prepare:</strong> decide what's worth fixing before you sell and what to skip. <strong>Buy &amp; Sell:</strong> buy the next home first when you can, or sell first when that fits your numbers better, and line up the financing. <strong>Move Once:</strong> move straight into the next home while the old one is prepped, listed, and sold.</p>
        </div>

        <VideoEmbed videoId={hubVideoId} title="Outgrown your home? Here's the plan" description="Jacob Stark explains the three-step plan for South Denver Metro homeowners who have outgrown their home." />

        <!-- SOUND FAMILIAR -->
        <div id="sound-familiar" style="padding-top: var(--space-xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Sound Familiar?</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">The Conversation Most Families Have Before They Call Me</h2>
          <TextThread label="A couple texting about whether to move" messages={[
            { from: 'them', text: "We need a bigger house." },
            { from: 'me', text: "But before we can buy a bigger house, we have to sell this one." },
            { from: 'them', text: "And before we sell this one, we probably need to fix some things." },
            { from: 'me', text: "But I don't know what to fix." },
            { from: 'me', text: "I don't know how much it'll cost." },
            { from: 'me', text: "I don't know if it's worth it." },
            { from: 'them', text: "And I don't know how we'd do all of that with work, kids, and life." },
            { from: 'me', text: "🤷", emoji: true },
          ]} />
          <p>If that's the loop you're stuck in, you're not behind and you're not doing anything wrong. Every decision depends on another one, so it's hard to know where to start. That's the part I take off your plate.</p>
          <p class="oyh-answer">Here's the plan. Here's what matters. Here's what doesn't. Here's how long it'll take. Here's what it will cost. Here's how we get from this house to the next one.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- THE PLAN -->
        <div id="the-plan" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">The Plan</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Prepare. Buy &amp; Sell. Move Once.</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">Three steps, built backward from the day you want to be in the new house.</p>
          <div class="process-steps">
            <div class="process-step">
              <h3>Prepare</h3>
              <p>We walk your house together. You get a straight answer on what's worth fixing, what to skip, what it should cost, and how long it takes, based on your home's condition and what buyers in your neighborhood are actually paying for. Then we build the timeline backward from your move-in date.</p>
              <p><a href={pillars.fixOrSkip.url}>{pillars.fixOrSkip.label} &rarr;</a></p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-step">
              <h3>Buy &amp; Sell</h3>
              <p>For most families, the easiest path is buying the next home first. We line up the funding so you can make a strong offer without a home-sale contingency and without carrying two full mortgages. If selling first fits your numbers better, we plan for that instead.</p>
              <p><a href={pillars.buyFirst.url}>{pillars.buyFirst.label} &rarr;</a></p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-step">
              <h3>Move Once</h3>
              <p>You move straight into the next home. Your old house gets refreshed, cleaned, and staged into its most inviting version, then listed. No showings to clean up for, and no second move. When it sells, the proceeds settle up whatever we used to get you there.</p>
              <p><a href={pillars.renovate.url}>{pillars.renovate.label} &rarr;</a></p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="section-cta">
            <p>Want your own version of this plan? Book 30 minutes and we'll map it out with your real numbers.</p>
            <a href={bookUrl} class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get Your Next-Move Plan</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- WHAT GETS IN THE WAY -->
        <div id="what-gets-in-the-way" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">What Gets in the Way</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">The Three Things That Keep Families Stuck</h2>
          <div class="oyh-blockers">
            <div class="oyh-blocker">
              <p class="oyh-blocker__quote">"We have to sell before we can buy."</p>
              <p>Not necessarily. Equity advances, bridge loans, and HELOCs can let you buy first. The right one depends on your equity and how much risk you're comfortable with. I'll show you the trade-offs side by side with your numbers.</p>
              <a href={pillars.buyFirst.url}>{pillars.buyFirst.label} &rarr;</a>
            </div>
            <div class="oyh-blocker">
              <p class="oyh-blocker__quote">"We need to fix things, but we don't know what."</p>
              <p>Most of what's stressing you won't change your sale price. A few things will. Knowing the difference is where I can save you real money, because I make these same calls on houses I buy and renovate with my own money.</p>
              <a href={pillars.fixOrSkip.url}>{pillars.fixOrSkip.label} &rarr;</a>
            </div>
            <div class="oyh-blocker">
              <p class="oyh-blocker__quote">"We can't manage contractors and showings with work and kids."</p>
              <p>You don't have to. Pre-listing updates can be managed for you, and some homeowners qualify to pay for them at closing instead of upfront. If you move out first, showings stop being your problem.</p>
              <a href={pillars.renovate.url}>{pillars.renovate.label} &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- OPTIONS TABLE -->
        <div id="your-options" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Your Options</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Buy First or Sell First? The Paths, Side by Side</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">There's no single right answer. Here's how the common paths compare for South Denver Metro homeowners.</p>
          <div class="oyh-table-wrap">
            <table class="oyh-table">
              <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Path</th><th scope="col">Best when</th><th scope="col">The trade-off</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Buy first with an equity advance</th><td>You have solid equity and want to move once and skip showings</td><td>Requires approval; program terms and costs vary</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Bridge loan or HELOC</th><td>You qualify to carry both payments for a while</td><td>Interest costs while both homes are owned; a HELOC usually has to be opened before you list</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Buy first with a sale-contingent offer</th><td>Sellers in your target neighborhood are accepting contingencies</td><td>Weaker offer; you can lose the house to a buyer without a contingency</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Sell first, then buy</th><td>You need every dollar of equity before you buy, or you'd rather not take on any extra financing</td><td>Possible rental or rent-back and a second move; pressure to find the next home quickly</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Guaranteed cash offer</th><td>Speed and certainty matter more than top dollar</td><td>Cash offers typically come in around 80&ndash;85% of market value</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-top: var(--space-sm); font-size: 0.9rem;"><a href={pillars.buyFirst.url}>How buying first works, what it covers, and how it can pay for itself &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>

        <!-- INVESTOR EYE / AUTHORITY -->
        <div id="investor-eye" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Realtor + Renovator</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Fix-or-Skip Advice From an Agent Who Renovates Homes With His Own Money</h2>
          <ul class="oyh-proof">
            <li><strong>Real renovation costs.</strong> I pay contractors on my own projects, so I know what the work should cost.</li>
            <li><strong>What buyers actually pay more for.</strong> I resell those homes, so I see which updates move the price and which don't.</li>
            <li><strong>Your house, not a checklist.</strong> Every call is based on your home's condition and what recent sales in your neighborhood show.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Most agents can tell you what your house might sell for. Fewer can tell you which projects will change that number, because they've never had to pay for the work themselves. I've been buying, renovating, and reselling homes as an investor since 2015. Every one of those projects forces the same question you're facing: is this worth doing, or will buyers never notice?</p>
          <p>That's the lens I bring to your house. Not a generic checklist, but a decision based on your home's condition, how the rest of the house compares, and what recent sales in your neighborhood say buyers will pay for.</p>

          <blockquote class="testimonial oyh-testimonial">
            <p class="testimonial__quote">Nothing but great things to say about our experience with Jacob! His communication, knowledge, expertise and dedication to our home sale and purchase were instrumental in helping us navigate the crazy Denver area market.</p>
            <p class="testimonial__author">Matthew S.</p>
            <p class="testimonial__detail">Centennial</p>
          </blockquote>
        </div>

        <!-- CALCULATOR -->
        <div id="equity-calculator" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Run Your Numbers</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">How Much Can You Put Toward the Next Home?</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">Get a directional read on your equity, your down payment, and your monthly cost on the next South Denver Metro home. No email required.</p>
          <HomeEquityCalculator showHeader={false} />
          <p style="margin-top: var(--space-md); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-body-text);">Want the detailed version? <a href="/tools/home-equity-calculator" style="color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline;">Open the full calculator</a>, or <a href={bookUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline;">book 30 minutes</a> and we'll run your real numbers together.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- AREAS -->
        <div id="areas-served" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Where I Help</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Moving Up Across the South Denver Metro</h2>
          <p>Jacob Stark helps homeowners who've outgrown their homes in every corner of the South Denver Metro, whether you're moving up within your neighborhood or trading a starter home in Englewood or Littleton for more space in Highlands Ranch, Centennial, or Parker.</p>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: var(--space-md);">
            <a href="/neighborhoods/littleton" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Littleton</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/highlands-ranch" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Highlands Ranch</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/centennial" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Centennial</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/englewood" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Englewood</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/parker" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Parker</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/lakewood" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Lakewood</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/lone-tree" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Lone Tree</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/castle-pines" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Castle Pines</a>
            <a href="/neighborhoods/greenwood-village" class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--sm">Greenwood Village</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Common Questions</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Outgrown Your Home? FAQ</h2>
          <div class="faq-list">
            {faqs.map((f) => (
              <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">{f.q}</button>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>{f.a}</p></div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>


        <!-- GO DEEPER (cluster nav) -->
        <div id="go-deeper" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Go Deeper</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Take the Next Step in the Plan</h2>
          <div class="oyh-blockers">
            <a class="oyh-blocker oyh-blocker--link" href={pillars.fixOrSkip.url}><p class="oyh-blocker__quote">Prepare: what to fix, what to skip</p><p>Which projects are worth doing before you list, and which ones buyers won't pay for.</p></a>
            <a class="oyh-blocker oyh-blocker--link" href={pillars.buyFirst.url}><p class="oyh-blocker__quote">Buy &amp; Sell: buy before you sell</p><p>How to buy your next home first, what the funding covers, and how it can pay for itself.</p></a>
            <a class="oyh-blocker oyh-blocker--link" href={pillars.renovate.url}><p class="oyh-blocker__quote">Move Once: updates with no money upfront</p><p>Get the old home refreshed, staged, and ready to sell, and pay for the work at closing.</p></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- RELATED -->
        {related.length > 0 && (
          <div id="related-reading" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
            <span class="section-label">Keep Reading</span>
            <h2 class="section-heading">More for Families Who've Outgrown Their Home</h2>
            <div class="card-grid">
              {related.map((p) => (
                <a href={`/blog/${p.id ?? p.slug}`} class="card">
                  <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__tag">{p.data.tag ?? 'Move-Up'}</span>
                    <h3 class="card__title">{p.data.title}</h3>
                    <p class="card__text">{p.data.description}</p>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        <!-- TRUST -->
        <div id="why-jacob" style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
          <span class="section-label">Why Jacob</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">The Track Record Behind the Plan</h2>
          <div class="trust-bar">
            <div class="trust-bar__item"><span class="trust-bar__value">{agent.stats.salesVolume}</span><span class="trust-bar__label">in Sales</span></div>
            <div class="trust-bar__item"><span class="trust-bar__value">{agent.stats.saleToList}</span><span class="trust-bar__label">Avg List-to-Close</span></div>
            <div class="trust-bar__item"><span class="trust-bar__value">{agent.stats.avgDaysOnMarket}</span><span class="trust-bar__label">Avg Days on Market</span></div>
            <div class="trust-bar__item"><span class="trust-bar__value">{agent.stats.familiesHelped}</span><span class="trust-bar__label">Families Helped</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CTA -->
  <section class="cta-banner" style="background-color: var(--color-white);">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="color: var(--color-dark-text);">You Don't Have to Figure This Out Alone</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-body-text);">In 30 minutes, we'll sort out what's worth fixing, whether to buy or sell first, and a realistic timeline to the next house. No pressure, no obligation.</p>
      <a href={bookUrl} class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get Your Next-Move Plan</a>
      <a href={agent.phoneHref} class="btn btn--outline-dark btn--lg">Call {agent.phone}</a>
    </div>
  </section>


  <PillarScripts />
</BaseLayout>
